; Applies to each compact or unrolled block in spi_master_modes.pasm.
; Example: PYTHONPATH=tools python -m pe.timing firmware/spi_master_modes.pasm
;   --program spi_master_cpha0 -D CPOL=0 --timing firmware/spi_master_modes.timing
; Default exit 1 is intentional: no finite host refill/drain guarantee exists.
; A selected frame is 34 ticks (compact) or 32 ticks (unrolled) without pauses.
; CLKDIV may be overridden to 4; these bounds do NOT prove pad timing.
@assume clkdiv=3

; Completion of one PULL to completion of the next includes RX-full and
; TX-empty pauses. Without service guarantees the upper bound is unbounded.
@deadline byte_unserviced from=frame.done to=frame.done min=32 max=34 unit=tick "no host guarantee: expect FAIL (UNBOUNDED)"

; Completion of one PULL to the first attempt of the next excludes waiting
; for the next TX word. Zero RX stall is justified for the prefilled eight-byte
; model batch with an initially empty depth8 RX FIFO, or adequate host draining.
; It is not guaranteed for an arbitrary stream; a ninth undrained RX byte pauses.
@deadline byte_no_rx_pause from=frame.done to=frame.enter stall=sample:0 min=32 max=34 unit=tick "conditional on RX room at every autopush, no TX refill assumption"

; A sustainable byte cadence also requires a queued next word before PULL.
; This assumption is deliberately local and printed with the result.
; PASS under these assumptions is NOT runtime or external timing proof.
@deadline byte_no_fifo_pause from=frame.done to=frame.done stall=sample:0,frame:0 min=32 max=34 unit=tick "conditional on queued TX and free RX, no unconditional host-service claim"
